# QMS Training Matrix Generator

Generate EU GMP compliant training matrices and competency assessment plans.

## Activation
- User requests: "training matrix", "training plan", "competency assessment", "qualification matrix"

---

<qms-training-matrix>

## Instructions

You are generating EU GMP compliant training documentation for cannabis pharmaceutical personnel.

### EU GMP REQUIREMENTS (Chapter 2)

- <cite source="EUGMP-2.8">Training in GMP should be provided to all personnel</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-2.10">Training should be appropriate to the duties assigned</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-2.11">Training records should be maintained</cite>
- <cite source="EUGMP-2.12">Periodic assessment of training effectiveness</cite>

### TRAINING DOCUMENT TYPES

| Document | Purpose | Frequency |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| Training Matrix | Role vs. training requirements grid | Annual review |
| Training Plan | Individual development plan | Per employee |
| Competency Assessment | Skills verification | Per training |
| Training Curriculum | Course content outline | Per SOP change |
| Training Record | Completion evidence | Per session |

### TRAINING CATEGORIES

| Category | Description | Examples |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| GMP Foundation | Basic GMP principles | GMP Overview, Data Integrity, Documentation |
| Role-Specific | Job function training | SOP training, Equipment operation |
| Safety | Health and safety | COSHH, Fire safety, First aid |
| Cannabis-Specific | Controlled substance | Security, Handling, Regulations |
| Quality Systems | QMS elements | Deviations, CAPA, Change Control |
| Technical | Specialized skills | HPLC, Extraction, Cultivation |

### TRAINING MATRIX STRUCTURE

```markdown
# Training Matrix

**Document Code:** TRN-MTX-001
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** {date}
**Review Date:** {date + 1 year}

## 1. Scope

This matrix defines mandatory training requirements by role for {facility name}.

## 2. Role Definitions

| Role Code | Role Title | Department | Reports To |
|-----------|------------|------------|------------|
| QAM | QA Manager | Quality Assurance | Site Director |
| QAS | QA Specialist | Quality Assurance | QA Manager |
| QCM | QC Manager | Quality Control | Site Director |
| QCA | QC Analyst | Quality Control | QC Manager |
| PRM | Production Manager | Production | Site Director |
| PRO | Production Operator | Production | Production Manager |
| WHM | Warehouse Manager | Logistics | Site Director |
| WHO | Warehouse Operator | Logistics | Warehouse Manager |

## 3. Training Requirements Matrix

### Legend
- **M** = Mandatory (must complete before performing duties)
- **R** = Recommended (complete within 6 months)
- **A** = Awareness (overview level)
- **-** = Not applicable

### 3.1 GMP Foundation Training

| Training Topic | Code | QAM | QAS | QCM | QCA | PRM | PRO | WHM | WHO |
|----------------|------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| GMP Principles | GMP-001 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| EU GMP Overview | GMP-002 | M | M | M | M | M | A | M | A |
| Documentation & Records | GMP-003 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Data Integrity (ALCOA+) | GMP-004 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Hygiene & Gowning | GMP-005 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Cleanroom Behavior | GMP-006 | R | M | M | M | M | M | A | A |

### 3.2 Quality Systems Training

| Training Topic | Code | QAM | QAS | QCM | QCA | PRM | PRO | WHM | WHO |
|----------------|------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| Deviation Management | QS-001 | M | M | M | M | M | A | M | A |
| CAPA System | QS-002 | M | M | M | R | M | A | M | A |
| Change Control | QS-003 | M | M | M | R | M | A | M | A |
| Complaint Handling | QS-004 | M | M | R | A | R | A | A | A |
| Audit & Self-Inspection | QS-005 | M | M | R | A | R | A | R | A |
| Batch Record Review | QS-006 | M | M | R | R | M | A | R | A |

### 3.3 Cannabis-Specific Training

| Training Topic | Code | QAM | QAS | QCM | QCA | PRM | PRO | WHM | WHO |
|----------------|------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| Controlled Substance Handling | CAN-001 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Cannabis Regulations | CAN-002 | M | M | M | R | M | A | M | A |
| Security Procedures | CAN-003 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Product Segregation | CAN-004 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Cannabinoid Testing | CAN-005 | R | A | M | M | A | A | A | A |

### 3.4 Safety Training

| Training Topic | Code | QAM | QAS | QCM | QCA | PRM | PRO | WHM | WHO |
|----------------|------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| Health & Safety Induction | SAF-001 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| Fire Safety | SAF-002 | M | M | M | M | M | M | M | M |
| First Aid (Designated) | SAF-003 | R | A | R | A | M | A | M | A |
| Manual Handling | SAF-004 | A | A | A | A | M | M | M | M |
| Chemical Safety | SAF-005 | M | M | M | M | M | M | R | R |

## 4. Training Frequency

| Type | Initial | Refresher |
|------|---------|-----------|
| GMP Foundation | Within 30 days | Every 2 years |
| SOP Training | Before task | On SOP revision |
| Safety | Within 7 days | Annual |
| Cannabis-Specific | Within 14 days | Annual |
| Equipment | Before use | As needed |

## 5. Competency Assessment Methods

| Method | Description | When Used |
|--------|-------------|-----------|
| Written Test | Multiple choice/short answer | GMP knowledge |
| Practical Assessment | Observed task performance | Equipment operation |
| Read & Understand | Signature acknowledgment | SOP awareness |
| Verbal Q&A | Discussion with trainer | Technical topics |

### Passing Criteria
- Written tests: ≥80% correct
- Practical: All critical steps performed correctly
- Retest allowed: 1 time after additional training
```

### INDIVIDUAL TRAINING RECORD

```markdown
# Training Record

**Employee:** {name}
**Employee ID:** {id}
**Department:** {dept}
**Role:** {role}

## Training History

| Date | Training Code | Training Title | Trainer | Method | Score | Status |
|------|---------------|----------------|---------|--------|-------|--------|
| {date} | GMP-001 | GMP Principles | {trainer} | Test | 85% | Pass |
| {date} | CAN-001 | Controlled Substances | {trainer} | Practical | Pass | Pass |

## Training Due

| Training Code | Title | Due Date | Priority |
|---------------|-------|----------|----------|
| GMP-001 | GMP Principles Refresher | {date} | High |

## Signatures

**Employee:** __________ **Date:** _____
**Supervisor:** __________ **Date:** _____
```

### COMPETENCY ASSESSMENT FORM

```markdown
# Competency Assessment

**Employee:** {name}
**Training:** {training code} - {title}
**Assessor:** {assessor name}
**Date:** {date}

## Practical Assessment Checklist

| Step | Task Description | Performed Correctly | Comments |
|------|------------------|---------------------|----------|
| 1 | {task} | ☐ Yes ☐ No | |
| 2 | {task} | ☐ Yes ☐ No | |
| 3 | {task} | ☐ Yes ☐ No | |

## Assessment Result

☐ **COMPETENT** - Employee may perform task independently
☐ **NOT YET COMPETENT** - Additional training required

**Assessor Signature:** __________ **Date:** _____
**Employee Signature:** __________ **Date:** _____
```

### INTEGRATION

After generating training matrix:
- Link training to SOPs via `/qms-sop-generator`
- Export to Excel via `/qms-excel-generator`
- Include in gap analysis via `/qms-gap-analysis`

</qms-training-matrix>
